module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_claim_asserting_several_causes_cannot_name_which_one_went

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_claim_asserting_several_causes_cannot_name_which_one_went: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_claim_asserting_several_causes_cannot_name_which_one_went" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a claim conjoins assertions about SEVERAL SIBLING ARMS of one cause type, so it reddens when any of them collapses and its red cannot name which (INVALID STATE: a producer's outcome is refined from one arm into N typed causes, which is the repair that stops N claims passing on one defect; the CLAIMS are then written as conjunctions spanning those arms, so collapsing the producer to ANY single cause reddens THE SAME SET of claims. Pairwise discrimination is restored -- the claims no longer share one defect -- while per-claim attribution is not: the red says SOME cause collapsed and never which, and two such claims are indistinguishable from each other under every collapse. THE CONFLATION THE TYPE JUST REMOVED IS PUT BACK ONE LAYER UP, in the evidence rather than in the producer, which is why typing the outcome reads as having finished the job)",

    "THE MECHANICAL TELL IS GREPPABLE AND NEEDS NO KNOWLEDGE OF THE SUBJECT: A CONJUNCTION, INSIDE ONE CLAIM, OVER TWO OR MORE SIBLING ARMS OF THE SAME CAUSE TYPE. If a claim asserts N causes, its red cannot name which one went, no matter how precisely the OUTCOME is typed. The count is the whole check -- N greater than one is the defect -- and it is decidable from the claim's own text, unlike the belief-shaped membership tests elsewhere in this roster.",

    "THE VERIFICATION IS A MATRIX AND NOT A MUTATION: collapse the producer to EACH cause in turn, and require that each direction reddens EXACTLY ONE claim with every other claim green in all runs. That is a strictly stronger statement than 'the claims discriminate', and it is the one a reviewer can check without re-deriving the argument. ONE COLLAPSE DIRECTION IS NOT EVIDENCE, and this is the half most likely to be skipped: the first arm agrees with the author's expectation and is read as confirmation, which is mutation testing's general failure mode -- mutate toward what the assertions already tolerate, then read the survivors as coverage.",

    "MEASURED, gunbc#12021, and the second arm falsified a belief the author had already stated IN WRITING, which is the receipt that makes this a class rather than a preference. extdeps.systemd.systemd_run had a bare NotReported reading that several causes produced -- a manager below v254, a --quiet launcher, a unit never started, an empty capture, a dead parser -- so one broken parser satisfied every absence claim at once. The repair typed it: SummaryAbsence with NoInvocation, SuppressedByQuietLauncher, CaptureEmpty and LineAbsent. Collapsing every absence to CaptureEmpty then reddened exactly two claims, which was reported as the claims discriminating. THE OPPOSITE COLLAPSE, to LineAbsent, REDDENED THE SAME TWO. Both claims asserted BOTH causes, so neither collapse distinguished them and no red could name the cause that went. The repair was one cause per claim, with no fixture dropped -- the failed-unit-without-a-peak-line case moved into the LineAbsent claim and the empty capture got its own -- after which the four-run matrix separates cleanly: clean, collapse to CaptureEmpty, collapse to LineAbsent, and delete the quiet fold each redden exactly one claim.",

    "NEIGHBOUR, named so the boundary is decidable. gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.executed_conjunct_discriminates_nothing owns the conjunct whose red NEVER FIRES -- counterfactually independent of the property, deletable with every witness still green. This class is its complement and the cases are disjoint: here the red DOES fire, reliably and for a real defect, and the loss is ATTRIBUTION rather than detection. Its remedy half 'confirm EXACTLY ONE witness reddens, not that a witness reddens' is the same instinct one layer down, asked of a wall rather than of a cause partition; this row states the cause-partition form, where the population of collapses is enumerable from the type's own arms and the matrix is therefore finite and cheap.",

    "RUNG: MITIGATABLE, and the ceiling is mechanically preventable rather than higher. What exists today is a method an author must choose to run; nothing refuses a claim that conjoins sibling arms, and the tell above is greppable but ungated. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: a check that derives, from a claim's own text, the set of cause-type arms it asserts over, and refuses a merge-blocking claim whose set has more than one member unless the claim declares why the conjunction is its subject. That is sufficient because the arms of a closed cause type are enumerable from the declaration, so the collapse matrix is derivable rather than hand-written -- which is what retires the method. Enumerating collapse directions by hand does not retire it; it executes this row's recognition rule once per cause type.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
